  "findings": [
    "Sparse independent receipt fills occur much later than the nominal3s threshold; the actual request delay is measured per fill.",
    "Raw observed later prices are causal but are not evidence that an already accepted production order would have remained unfilled until that later receipt.",
    "Profit-target sell limits prevent adverse below-target fills: a failed target remains open and later stop handling occurs only once the pending target expires.",
    "Loss-limit/two-hour exit is an intent trigger, not a guaranteed worst-loss/holding-time bound. Limit orders can remain unfilled as prices fall; final stale liquidation is null rather than zero.",
    "Publication boundaries cancel local counterfactual pending intents while preserving inventory; not evidence of production order cancellation.",
    "Two4tick wins in the same market are correlated and cannot establish scale profitability."
  ],
